, "lp": -0.0001263698359252885, "top": [[" C", -0.0001263698359252885], [" `", -9.601944923400879]]}, {"t": "Make", "lp": -0.0009521605097688735, "top": [["Make", -0.0009521605097688735], ["make", -7.227287769317627]]}, {"t": " to", "lp": -6.950143142603338e-05, "top": [[" to", -6.950143142603338e-05], [" which", -10.889558792114258]]}, {"t": " generate", "lp": -0.11805195361375809, "top": [[" generate", -0.11805195361375809], [" use", -2.198568820953369]]}, {"t": " build", "lp": -0.5783883929252625, "top": [[" build", -0.5783883929252625], [" **", -0.9183560609817505]]}, {"t": " files", "lp": -0.31840625405311584, "top": [[" files", -0.31840625405311584], [" scripts", -1.4795753955841064]]}, {"t": " for", "lp": -0.04028143733739853, "top": [[" for", -0.04028143733739853], [" using", -3.6793577671051025]]}, {"t": " **", "lp": -0.291446715593338, "top": [[" **", -0.291446715593338], [" the", -1.3787708282470703]]}], "text": "Here is a step-by-step breakdown of the `build()` function in your PKGBUILD.\n\n### 1. Environment Setup\n```bash\nsource /opt/intel/oneapi/setvars.sh --force\n```\n*   **Purpose:** This script sets up the environment variables required for Intel OneAPI tools (compilers, libraries, paths).\n*   **`--force`:** This flag forces the script to overwrite existing environment variables. This is crucial in Arch Linux packaging because `makepkg` might have set some variables (like `PATH` or `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`) that could conflict with OneAPI's expectations. Forcing it ensures the OneAPI environment is clean and correct.\n\n### 2. Error Handling\n```bash\nset -e\n```\n*   **Purpose:** This is a standard Bash safety measure. It tells the shell to **exit immediately** if any command returns a non-zero exit code (an error).\n*   **Why it's here:** Without this, if `cmake` fails, the script might continue trying to run `ninja` or other commands, leading to confusing errors or incomplete builds. With `set -e`, the build stops at the first failure.\n\n### 3. CMake Configuration\n```bash\ncmake -S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\" -B \"${srcdir}/build\" -G Ninja \\\n```\n*   **`-S \"${srcdir}/llama.cpp\"`:** Specifies the **source directory**. This is where the downloaded git repository lives.\n*   **`-B \"${srcdir}/build\"`:** Specifies the **build directory**. CMake will generate all intermediate files (Makefiles, Ninja files, object files) here. This keeps the source tree clean.\n*   **`-G Ninja`:** Tells CMake to generate build files for **"}